        {
          "question": "e-5155",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)^n} = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2}  +  \\cdots .\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=3a$ and $n=5$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+3a)}^{5} & =1+5(3a)+\\frac{5(5-1)}{2!}{(3a)}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+5(3a)+\\frac{5(4)}{2}(9{a}^{2})+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+15a+90{a}^{2}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
