      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-9778",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The binomial expansion for $(1 + x)^n$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1 + x)^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{n(n - 1)}{2!} x^2 + \\cdots .\n$$\n\nIn particular, the $x^3$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!} x^3.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3r$ and $n$ with $10$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10(10-1)(10-2)}{3!}(-3r)^{3} & =\\frac{10(9)(8)}{6}\\cdot (-3)^{3}\\cdot {r}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(9)(8)}{6}\\cdot (-27){r}^{3} \\\\  & =-3\\,240{r}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $r^3$ is $-3\\,240.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-9778.json",
          "file_sha256": "4b5187b7ee355772275747400eec06052e3dea53685618c188223ea751b79c8e"
        }
